D = {
 'Alagondar Scion|IDROTF': "Secret. You are the last known heir of the Alagondar line and of Neverwinter's crown. If Dagult Neverember, the lord-regent, learns you live, he will send assassins to kill you.",
 'Anvilwrought|MOT': "You were forged at Purphoros's forge and have a metallic sheen and visible joints.\n\n**Constructed Resilience.** Advantage on saves against being poisoned and resistance to poison damage. You need no food, drink, air, or sleep, and magic can't put you to sleep. Immune to disease.\n\n**Sentry's Rest.** On a long rest, you spend 6 hours inactive and motionless instead of sleeping. You stay conscious and can see and hear.",
 'Deep Delver|OOTA': 'You can always retrace your steps underground and know whether Underdark food and water are safe. In the Underdark, you can find enough food and water for yourself and up to five others, if any sustenance exists in the area.',
 'Doppelganger|IDROTF': "Secret. You are a shapechanger with none of the traits of the race you imitate. You keep your class features, background, and alignment. You have darkvision 60 feet. As an action, cast detect thoughts at will with no components (Intelligence, DC 8 + proficiency bonus + Intelligence modifier), or polymorph into a humanoid you have seen, or back. Only size changes. Gear doesn't. You revert at death.",
 'Drizzt Fan|IDROTF': "Secret. You once met the drow ranger Drizzt Do'Urden. You keep a tattered scrap of his green cloak and will never give it up.",
 'Echoing Soul|VRGR': "Dark Gift. Echoes of another life grant knowledge you can't explain. A Soul Echoes table gives its nature.\n\n**Channeled Prowess.** Proficiency in two skills of your choice.\n\n**Inherent Tongue.** One extra language.\n\n**Intrusive Echoes.** When you roll a 1 on a d20 for an attack, check, or save, roll on a table for a bad or good effect. Then it can't recur until a short or long rest.",
 'Elusive Paramour|IDROTF': 'Secret. A wealthy pasha in Calimshan put a bounty on you for seducing his favorite concubine. Bounty hunters search the Sword Coast, and you hope they never look in Icewind Dale.',
 'Escaped Prisoner|IDROTF': 'Secret. Spacefaring mind flayers took you from another world. Their ship crashed in the mountains south of Ten-Towns. You crossed the tundra and nearly froze before friendly trappers found you. Some captors may have survived and may hunt for you.',
 'Gathered Whispers|VRGR': 'Unseen spirits whisper around you. A table sets what haunts you.\n\n**Spirit Whispers.** Learn message, no components. Casting ability: Int, Wis, or Cha.\n\n**Sudden Cacophony.** When hit by an attack, use your reaction to add your proficiency bonus to AC against it. After it causes a miss, recharge on a long rest.\n\n**Voices from Beyond.** On a d20 roll of 1, roll for an effect. It recurs after a rest.',
 'Heroic Destiny|MOT': 'Great deeds lie ahead of you. Choose or roll a destiny on a table.\n\n**Defy Death.** Advantage on death saving throws.\n\n**Hard to Kill.** When reduced to 0 hit points but not killed outright, you can drop to 1 hit point instead. Once used, it recharges on a long rest.',
 'Hollow One|EGW': "Blightshore magic fills the void left by your soul.\n\n**Ageless.** You don't age.\n\n**Cling to Life.** A death save of 16 or higher restores 1 hit point.\n\n**Revenance.** You keep your type but register as undead to detection.\n\n**Unsettling Presence.** As an action, a creature within 15 feet has disadvantage on its next save within 1 minute. Constructs, undead, and creatures immune to fright are immune. Long rest recharge.",
 'Iconoclast|MOT': "You deny the gods and resist them. Wisdom is your casting ability.\n\n**Enlightened Protection.** Cast protection from evil and good on yourself, no materials. Long rest recharge.\n\n**Reject the Gods.** You can't gain or lose piety. Once per long rest each: dispel magic at 5th level, dispel evil and good at 11th (dispel magic then 4th level), antimagic field at 17th (dispel magic then 5th level).",
 'Inheritor|VRGR': 'You inherit the legacy of a famed ancestor or mentor and hold a token that marks you as their heir, such as a ring, garment, or weapon. When you reveal your legacy, you quickly learn what locals think of your predecessor. If they know them, many see you as a hero or a threat. Heroes can gain an audience with local leaders, and threats are urged to leave.',
 'Inscrutable|MOT': "Your mind is a maze, impenetrable like a sphinx's. A table suggests why.\n\n**Psychic Shield.** Resistance to psychic damage.\n\n**Sphinx's Shroud.** You are immune to effects that sense your emotions or read your thoughts. Wisdom (Insight) checks to judge your intentions or sincerity have disadvantage.",
 'Lifelong Companion|MOT': "Your greatness comes from supporting others. A table suggests your legendary bond. Any tie to another player's character needs that player's consent.\n\n**Boon Aura.** While you aren't incapacitated, allies within 5 feet have advantage on saves against being frightened or charmed.\n\n**Companion's Protection.** When a creature you see within 5 feet is hit by an attack, use your reaction to take the hit instead. Recharges on a long rest.",
 'Littlest Yeti|IDROTF': 'Secret. Yeti raised you. You relied on them for food and warmth but never adapted to cold. You speak Yeti and have advantage on Charisma checks to influence yeti or improve their attitude.',
 'Living Shadow|VRGR': 'Your shadow moves on its own. A table gives its quirk. Casting ability: Int, Wis, or Cha.\n\n**Grasping Shadow.** Learn mage hand, no components.\n\n**Shadow Strike.** Add 10 feet of reach to a melee attack, proficiency bonus times per long rest.\n\n**Ominous Will.** On a d20 roll of 1, the next roll by you or a creature within 30 feet gets a d4 (odd subtracts, even adds). Once per rest.',
 'Midwinter Child|IDROTF': 'Secret. Auril the Frostmaiden blessed you, since you were born on the Midwinter holiday. You have resistance to cold damage.',
 'Mist Walker|VRGR': 'You slip through the Mists but they drain you if you linger. Casting ability: Int, Wis, or Cha.\n\n**Misty Step.** Cast misty step once per long rest, no slot.\n\n**Mist Traveler.** Reach a named domain as if you held its Mist talisman.\n\n**Poisoned Roots.** After a long rest, you are safe in the area (10 miles) for weeks equal to your Con modifier (min. 1). Then each long rest needs a DC 15 Con save or 1 exhaustion.',
 'Mist Wanderer|VRGR': 'The Mists guide you. You immediately know if an object you touch is a Mist talisman. If you have visited its domain of origin, you know where it comes from.',
 'Nyxborn|MOT': 'You are an idea given life by the gods in Nyx. Tables suggest your origin and quirks.\n\n**Cloak of Stars.** As an action, wrap yourself in a starry cloak for 1 minute. Attack rolls against you have disadvantage. You can doff it freely. Recharges on a long rest.\n\n**Nyxborn Resistance.** Resistance to necrotic and radiant damage.',
 'Old Flame|IDROTF': "Secret. You have a lover in Ten-Towns you haven't seen in years. Outside combat, you can pick an NPC in Ten-Towns you can see as that lover. You can't change the choice. The old flame is friendly and helpful, even if your past was rocky.",
 'Oracle|MOT': "You speak with the gods but receive dire insights. A table gives your curse. Wisdom is your casting ability.\n\n**Ears of the Oracle.** Speak Celestial. A god may speak through you.\n\n**Oracle's Insight.** Add a d10 to an ability check, even after rolling. Short or long rest recharge.\n\n**Oracle's Piety.** Piety 3: ritual augury. 10: divination. 25: commune, and you can't be surprised. 50: +2 Int or Wis.",
 'Orc Stone|IDROTF': 'Secret. You saved an orc, who gave you a Many-Arrows tribe stone. It is an uncommon magic item that only you can attune to. As an action, summon an orc war chief spirit within 30 feet. It obeys you and lasts 10 minutes or until it drops to 0 hit points. After three uses, the stone turns to dust.',
 'Owlbear Whisperer|IDROTF': 'Secret. Owlbears tend to like you. Within 10 feet of one, you can use an action to make a DC 10 Charisma (Animal Handling) check. On a success, its attitude shifts from hostile to indifferent or from indifferent to friendly.',
 'Pious|MOT': 'You have a bond with a god since birth. A table suggests your faith quirks.\n\n**Pious Protection.** When you fail a saving throw, reroll it and use the new roll. Recharges on a long rest.\n\n**Religious Study.** Advantage on Intelligence (Religion) checks about your chosen god.\n\n**Starting Piety.** You begin with piety 3 with that god.',
 'Pirate Cannibal|IDROTF': 'Secret. You served on Dark Duchess, a Luskan pirate ship. When it froze in the ice, all but the captain fled toward Ten-Towns and got lost in a blizzard. You alone survived, by eating your mates. The ship and its treasure are still out there.',
 'Reghed Heir|IDROTF': 'Secret. You are the child of Queen Bjornhild Solvigsdottir of the Tiger Tribe. She cast you into the Sea of Moving Ice as a sacrifice to Auril. A polar bear saved you, then became a goliath named Oyaminartok who took you to Ten-Towns. You owe her your life and owe your mother a merciless death.',
 'Reincarnation|IDROTF': "Secret. A friendly human druid brought you back from death with reincarnate. You never learned the druid's name or fate. You keep memories of your past life, spent partly in Icewind Dale. Roll on the spell's table for your prior race or choose one, then build that story.",
 'Ring Hunter|IDROTF': "Secret. A trout bit off your father's finger, with his signet ring on it. You hunt that fish to recover the ring and keep your inheritance.",
 'Runaway Author|IDROTF': "Secret. You wrote the exposé The Hellbent Highborn, accusing patriars of Baldur's Gate and nobles of Waterdeep of devil worship. Your claims were true, but you made many enemies and fled to Icewind Dale.",
 'Second Skin|VRGR': 'Another side of you has a second form. A table gives it. Casting ability: Int, Wis, or Cha.\n\n**Transformation.** Cast alter self (Change Appearance only) with no slot once per long rest, or with slots. A visible mark lasts until a long rest.\n\n**Involuntary Change.** After a catalyst, at your next turn start pass a DC 15 Charisma save or use your action to cast it.',
 'Slaad Host|IDROTF': "Secret. A red slaad implanted an egg in you before you began adventuring. If you can't remove it within two months, a slaad tadpole bursts from your chest and kills you. It then grows into an adult slaad and kills others.",
 'Spirit Medium|VRGR': 'You serve as a conduit for spirits. You have advantage on Arcana or Religion checks to recall or research spirits and the afterlife. You start with a custom divining device, such as a spirit board, tarokka deck, planchette, dowsing rods, or tea cup. Add your proficiency bonus to ability checks made with it.',
 'Spy|IDROTF': 'Secret. You are a Harper spy guarding Ten-Towns while hiding your ties. Threats include the Arcane Brotherhood of Luskan wizards and the Zhentarim shadow network. Your only contact is Beldora, a human posing as a homeless woman who gathers information in Bryn Shander.',
 'Symbiotic Being|VRGR': 'A being shares your body and returns at midnight if severed.\n\n**Entwined Existence.** It has Int, Wis, and Cha, shares your senses, speaks two languages, and grants one skill proficiency. It dies and revives with you.\n\n**Sustained Symbiosis.** After a failed save, spend a Hit Die and add the roll. Death saves succeed. Long rest recharge.\n\n**Symbiotic Agenda.** Ignore its goal and resist a DC 12 + its Cha modifier Charisma save or be charmed 1d12 hours.',
 'Touch of Death|VRGR': 'Your touch harms. A table gives its source.\n\n**Death Touch.** As an action, make an unarmed strike that deals extra 1d10 necrotic damage (2d10 at 5th level, 3d10 at 11th, 4d10 at 17th).\n\n**Inescapable Death.** Your necrotic damage ignores resistance.\n\n**Withering Contact.** At your turn start, a creature grappling you or grappled by you takes 1d10 necrotic damage.',
 'Trauma Survivor|VRGR': 'You survived a traumatic situation and can help others. People see you as an expert on it. You know nonmagical recovery methods, common resources, and misinformation. You can persuade sympathetic doctors, clergy, and local leaders to shelter one other person at a modest lifestyle for up to one month.',
 'Traveler|VRGR': "You come from a place others can't grasp. Among sympathetic caravans, itinerant families, or displaced groups, you can find a place to hide, rest, or recuperate unless you seem dangerous. They hide you from the law and pursuers but won't risk their lives for you. You can tell whether a nearby object you touch comes from your homeland.",
 'Underdark Experience|OOTA': 'You have spent long in the Underdark and know its races, civilizations, settlements, and major routes. If you fail an Intelligence check to recall Underdark lore, you know a source to consult, unless the DM rules the lore is unknown.',
 'Unscarred|MOT': 'You resist physical harm like the hero Haktos. A table gives the origin.\n\n**Unscarred Resilience.** When you take damage, use your reaction to roll a d12, add your Constitution modifier, and reduce the damage by that total. Recharges on a short or long rest.',
 'Watchers|VRGR': "Malicious shadow spirits, usually Tiny beasts, follow you and always return.\n\n**Borrowed Eyes.** As an action for 1 hour, advantage on Investigation and Perception checks and can't be blinded. Long rest recharge.\n\n**Dread Presence.** Disadvantage on Deception, Performance, and Persuasion against those who see them, and on saves against scrying. A minute and DC 15 Charisma (Animal Handling) check suppresses both for 1 hour, once per long rest.",
}
